# Sotto Reads — local development configuration
#
# Production cloud voice goes through the standalone Cloudflare Worker
# (`worker/`), which owns the OpenRouter key. Nothing in this file is needed
# for the deployed site.
#
# Local development has two options:
#   1. Point VITE_TTS_API_BASE at the deployed Worker (recommended), or
#   2. Copy this file to `.env.local` and use the Vite proxy with a local key.
#
# Never commit `.env.local`. Keys are read server-side only.

# Optional: use the deployed Worker from `npm run dev`
# VITE_TTS_API_BASE=https://sotto-tts.spectaculardipin.workers.dev

# Option A — OpenRouter (recommended for development)
# Uses the free Fish Audio S2.1 Pro endpoint by default:
#   fish-audio/s2.1-pro-free:free
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Optional: override the OpenRouter TTS model
# OPENROUTER_TTS_MODEL=fish-audio/s2.1-pro-free:free
# Optional: only for models that require a named voice
# OPENROUTER_TTS_VOICE=

# Option B — Fish Audio directly (gives exact word-level timings)
FISH_API_KEY=
# Optional: override the Fish model
# FISH_MODEL=s2.1-pro-free

# Which cloud provider to use when both keys exist: fish | openrouter
# TTS_DEFAULT_PROVIDER=fish

# Offline UI/audio-pipeline testing with a generated tone voice.
# Remove this line for real cloud audio.
# TTS_MOCK=1
# Optional delay per mock batch, useful for watching the queue fill.
# TTS_MOCK_DELAY_MS=900
